  "output": {
    "section_id": "ch01.s02",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "ch01.s02.p01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p01.01",
            "text": "How do large language models fit into the wider landscape of AI, and why are they only one part of generative AI?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p01.02",
            "text": "Generative AI is broader than large language models, and it includes language, video, audio, and 3D models.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@489",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@490",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@495",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@497",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@500",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@503",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@506"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p01.03",
            "text": "Examples shown for generative AI include realistic videos that are made by artificial intelligence rather than shot on camera.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@511",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@514",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@519",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@522",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@524",
              "Xpr8D6LeAtw@527"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p01.04",
            "text": "A large language model, by contrast, is a neural network designed to understand, generate, and respond to human-like text.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@153",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@157",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@160",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@164",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@168",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@170",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@172",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@174"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p01.05",
            "text": "At the core, LLMs are neural networks built for generic text-related applications such as understanding, generating, and responding to human-like text.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@232",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@235",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@241",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@243",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@245",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@360",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@362"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p01.06",
            "text": "They can also be described as deep neural networks trained on massive amounts of data to do tasks such as understanding, generating, and responding to human-like text.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@366",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@369",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@371",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@374",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@377",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@379"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch01.s02.p02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p02.01",
            "text": "To make that definition concrete, it helps to unpack what a neural network is.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p02.02",
            "text": "A neural network takes input data, feeds it into a layer of neurons, stacks a number of these layers together, and produces an output layer.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@189",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@192",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@193",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@197",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@199"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p02.03",
            "text": "The name \"neural network\" comes from the idea that these neurons represent the circuitry in the brain in a very symbolic sense.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@201",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@204",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@206",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@210"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p02.04",
            "text": "Deep neural networks have many applications, including image detection, text generation, self-driving cars, and detecting whether a patient has a brain tumor.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@213",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@215",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@218",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@220",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@223",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@226",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@229",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@230"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p02.05",
            "text": "LLMs are one specific application of these deep learning techniques, focused on processing and generating human-like text.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@1516",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@1520",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@1522",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@1524",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@1526",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@1528"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p02.06",
            "text": "They are called language models because they deal with language rather than other modalities such as images or video.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@656",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@659",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@665",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@667",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@669",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@672"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch01.s02.p03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p03.01",
            "text": "The word \"large\" adds another part of the definition.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p03.02",
            "text": "In \"large language model,\" \"large\" refers to the number of parameters in the model.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@417",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@421",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@423",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@426",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@428"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p03.03",
            "text": "LLMs typically have billions of parameters, and some have trillions of parameters.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@432",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@433",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@435",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@439",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@441",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@445",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@447",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@450"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p03.04",
            "text": "A table of GPT-3 model sizes ranges from 125 million parameters through 350 million, 760 million, 13 billion, and up to 175 billion parameters, and GPT-4 is said to have even more parameters.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@455",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@457",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@460",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@464",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@466",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@469",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@472",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@477",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@481",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@492",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@495"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p03.05",
            "text": "As models progress from GPT-1 to GPT-2 to GPT-3, they become better and their parameter counts increase tremendously.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@501",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@503",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@508",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@511",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@513",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@515",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@526",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@529",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@533",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@536"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p03.06",
            "text": "The same comparison also shows other quantities increasing as the models grow: GPT-1 has 12 decoders, GPT-2 has 48, GPT-3 has 96, and token size increases from 512 to 1024 to 2048.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@540",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@541",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@543",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@551",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@554",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@558",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@562",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@564",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@566"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s02.p03.07",
            "text": "A separate graph covering 1950 to 2022 shows model parameter counts growing from very small values in early decades to around 100 million, 1 billion, and almost 1 trillion by around 2020, with language models among the largest.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@568",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@570",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@573",
              "3dWzNZXA8DY@575",
